3a:["$","div","7",{"className":"p-6 rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-lg mb-3","children":"What Western philosophy is closest to Advaita?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"Spinoza's pantheism, Hegel's Absolute Idealism, and aspects of Neoplatonism are frequently compared. Schopenhauer explicitly studied Upanishadic thought. However, Indian non-duality includes specific meditative practices absent from Western counterparts."}]]}]
